  "abstract": "Kōgo ian kaishū is a Japanese manuscript of medical cases in two parts bound as one volume. It opens with a dated assignment and records cases in a mixture of kanji and katakana. Formula names accompanied by passages introduced as comments show how case narratives, prescriptions and criticism were arranged. The manuscript offers evidence for the study of case writing and case-based medical instruction in historical Japan. This dataset uses 21 fixed images from the Fujikawa Collection, Kyoto University Main Library, record RB00002360. The main text is transcribed from 19 pages. The AI-reviewed JSON, TXT and TEI transcription records 594 unresolved comparison items from the primary review. Full human collation is outstanding.",
